ORIGIN OF DESIGN
----------------
dorang is an independent Go implementation. It was informed by the following
works. No source code was copied from any of them; mechanisms were re-implemented
from analysis of their published behavior and interfaces.

  Jikji — https://github.com/jikji-labs/jikji
    Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Jioh L. Jung
    Provider-backbone concepts: multi-axis capacity brokering, credential pool
    rotation, sticky routing, provider-reported usage-limit normalization,
    provider-kind defaults and model-prefix capability inference.
    Used by the same copyright holder; contributed to dorang under Apache-2.0.

  OpenClaw — https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw — MIT License
    Copyright (c) 2026 OpenClaw Foundation
    Provider-catalog / plugin-manifest structure.

  Hermes Agent — https://github.com/nousresearch/hermes-agent — MIT License
    Copyright (c) 2025 Nous Research
    Provider-profile concept for mapping a neutral reasoning configuration onto
    provider-specific wire representations.

Interoperability with the LiteLLM proxy configuration format and with the
OpenAI, Anthropic, and vLLM HTTP APIs is implemented from their public wire
formats for compatibility purposes.

Third-party Go modules retain their respective copyright and license notices;
see the generated dependency attribution material in release artifacts.
